; link/pop_cels_res.link — the PINNED page of the split cel image (P3.78).
;
; Supersedes link/pop_cels.link, which linked the whole image as one unit at $C000. The
; scene outgrew that: 39,682 B of cels against a bank that is 31,744 B addressable, so
; the image is cut into a pinned page and five rotating ones (harness/tools/cel_pack.py).
;
; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
; WHAT LIVES HERE, AND WHY IT IS THE HALF THAT DOES NOT MOVE.
; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
; $C000 is reached through $FFA6, and this page stays mapped for the entire scene. It
; carries the magic, the bounds, the [cel][facing][phase] table, and the cels that must
; be reachable when no particular rotating page is:
;
;   * the standing cels the two song holds draw — pinning those is precisely what makes
;     a hold a place a disk read can hide, because the rotating block is then free;
;   * the cels the packer had to pin to bring an over-large beat under one block (Pback
;     draws 9,538 B and a rotating block holds 7,680);
;   * the terminal beat's cels, which hold forever and which no later read can renew.
;
; The TABLE is why the pin exists at all. co_variant consults it on every cel it places,
; so it has to be mapped at every instant; rotating both window registers would mean a
; copy of it in every page — 1,360 B duplicated five times, and a second home for a fact
; whose whole design is that it has one.
;
; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
; THE `load` VALUE IS BARE HEX, AND $C000 WOULD SILENTLY LINK AT ZERO.
; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
; `section prog load $C000` parses the `$` form as 0 — no error, no warning, exit 0, and
; the image lands at $0000. Same shape of silence as lwasm's `-D` taking a $-prefixed
; value as zero (build.bat documents that one). It is caught rather than trusted:
; decb_to_raw.py refuses an image whose first segment is not exactly at the `--base`
; build.bat states.
;
; Comments here are `;`. lwlink does NOT accept `*` — that is an assembler convention and
; using it is a parse error, not a comment.

section prog load C000

entry cel_image
